# Keep the PUBLIC docker image clean: never let real credentials enter the build context.
# The Dockerfile's `COPY fields/SECRETS*.json /app/` then matches ONLY SECRETS.example.json (the inert
# placeholder), so the docker image is clean even if someone forgets the move-aside-during-build step.
# NOTE: the .sif is built by Singularity/Apptainer, which does NOT read this file — it still bakes the
# real fields/SECRETS.json via the .def %files section (that's intended; the .sif is never pushed public).
SECRETS.json
**/SECRETS.json
*presigned*

# Build-context trimming — none of the below are COPY'd into the image; excluding them just speeds builds.
*.sif
fields/NII_debug/
output/
**/__pycache__/
.git/
